l moves from Halych to Kholm.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_of_Galicia","c":3},{"y":1245,"t":"gain","x":"August 1245: Daniel takes the rest of Galicia.","m":8,"cp":"principality-of-chernigov","cpn":"Principality of Chernigov","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_of_Galicia","c":2},{"y":1253,"t":"rename","x":"1253: Daniel crowned King of Ruthenia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":3},{"y":1260,"t":"loss","x":"1260: Mongol authority imposed.","cp":"mongol-empire","cpn":"Mongol Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":1},{"y":1272,"t":"capital_move","x":"1272: Lev I moves the capital from Chelm to Lviv.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":3},{"y":1276,"t":"loss","x":"1276: Lithuania takes Black Ruthenia.","cp":"grand-duchy-of-lithuania","cpn":"Grand Duchy of Lithuania","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_I_of_Galicia","c":1},{"y":1280,"t":"gain","x":"1280: Leo annexes part of Carpathian Ruthenia.","cp":"kingdom-of-hungary","cpn":"Kingdom of Hungary","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_I_of_Galicia","c":2},{"y":1292,"t":"gain","x":"1292: Lev reaches into the Lublin region.","cp":"duchy-of-sandomierz","cpn":"Duchy of Sandomierz","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":2},{"y":1301,"t":"loss","x":"1301: Transcarpathia back to Hungary.","cp":"kingdom-of-hungary","cpn":"Kingdom of Hungary","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_I_of_Galicia","c":1},{"y":1302,"t":"loss","x":"1302: Yuri I loses Lublin.","cp":"kingdom-of-poland","cpn":"Kingdom of Poland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":3},{"y":1302,"t":"capital_move","x":"The seat passes from Lviv to Volodymyr after Lev I's death.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuri_I_of_Galicia","c":2},{"y":1323,"t":"rename","x":"1323: the Rurikid line ends.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":2},{"y":1326,"t":"loss","x":"1326: the northern strip goes to Lithuania.","cp":"grand-duchy-of-lithuania","cpn":"Grand Duchy of Lithuania","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":1},{"y":1340,"t":"contest_start","x":"June 1340: Casimir III takes Lviv.","m":6,"cp":"kingdom-of-poland","cpn":"Kingdom of Poland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia_Wars","c":3},{"y":1344,"t":"loss","x":"1344: Peremyshl goes to Poland.","cp":"kingdom-of-poland","cpn":"Kingdom of Poland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":3},{"y":1349,"t":"contest_end","x":"1349: Casimir III annexes Galicia.","cp":"kingdom-of-poland","cpn":"Kingdom of Poland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":3},{"y":1349,"t":"loss","x":"1349: Galicia passes to the Polish Crown; the vassalage to the Golden Horde ended.","cp":"kingdom-of-poland","cpn":"Kingdom of Poland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":3},{"y":1349,"t":"loss","x":"1349: Volhynia goes to Lithuania.","cp":"grand-duchy-of-lithuania","cpn":"Grand Duchy of Lithuania","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":2},{"y":1349,"t":"dissolve","x":"1349: the Kingdom of Galicia-Volhynia ends.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Roman's Cuman campaigns","from":1201,"to":1204,"outcome":"'In 1201-1202 and 1203-1204 Roman led two successful campaigns against the Cumans'; no land changed hands on the page.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_the_Great"},{"name":"War of the Galician Succession","from":1205,"to":1245,"outcome":"Roman's death in 1205 began the war 'in 1205 and ran to 1245' (Roman page).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_the_Great"},{"name":"Mongol invasion of Kievan Rus'","from":1237,"to":1241,"outcome":"Mongol victory; Kiev stormed in December 1240.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasion_of_Kievan_Rus%27"},{"name":"Daniel's wars with Kuremsa and Burundai","from":1254,"to":1260,"outcome":"Daniel drove the Mongols out of Volhynia in 1256 and held Lutsk and Volodymyr in 1257, but in 1259-1260 Burundai's and Boroldai's armies made him pull down his fortifications and accept Mongol authority.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia"},{"name":"Lithuanian-Galician war of 1274-1276","from":1274,"to":1276,"outcome":"'Leo fought a war against the new Lithuanian ruler, Traidenis, but was defeated'; Lithuania took Black Ruthenia and Navahrudak.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_I_of_Galicia"},{"name":"Leo's campaigns against Poland and Hungary","from":1279,"to":1280,"outcome":"In 1279 Leo allied with Wenceslaus II of Bohemia and invaded Poland; the attempt on Krakow failed in 1280.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_I_of_Galicia"},{"name":"Galicia-Volhynia Wars","from":1340,"to":1392,"outcome":"Fall of the Kingdom of Galicia-Volhynia: Casimir took Lviv in June 1340; a 1344 treaty gave Galicia to Casimir and Volhynia to Liubartas; Poland took Galicia (1349 on the Kingdom page), Hungary held it 1370-1387, and the 1392 Ostrow agreement left Poland…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia_Wars"}],"certainty":[{"from":1199,"to":1349,"level":"soft","note":"No border of the kingdom is given by a survey or a line on any page opened; the Peremyshl cut of 1344 and the 1302 loss of Lublin are named by treaty or event but without boundaries."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia","title":"Kingdom of Galicia-Volhynia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_of_Galicia","title":"Daniel of Galicia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_the_Great","title":"Roman the Great"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasion_of_Kievan_Rus%27","title":"Mongol invasion of Kievan Rus'"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_I_of_Galicia","title":"Leo I of Galicia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuri_I_of_Galicia","title":"Yuri I of Galicia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boleslaw-Yuri_II_of_Galicia","title":"Boleslaw-Yuri II of Galicia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia_Wars","title":"Galicia-Volhynia Wars"}]}